The organisation applies the basic security practices in the IT and the cloud services that it runs: multi-factor authentication, updates, secure configuration, malware protection, network segmentation, separate administrator accounts, logging, backups, encryption, and secured communications.

== How to decide if this control is required

This control is required when the organisation runs IT or cloud services itself, or administers the services that it uses. NIS2 requires these practices (Article 21(2)(g), (h), and (j)). If a supplier runs the services, check the practices from the agreement and the reports of the supplier.

== How to implement

Check the practices once a year with the checklist in the evidence. The checklist follows the basic hygiene practices that Traficom recommends for NIS2 entities. The checklist also covers the safe use of AI tools. Fix the gaps, or create a task for each gap. The cryptography rules are evidence of the control "Set the information security policy".

